      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'How It Works') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            Scale modifiers set <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">--modifier-scale</code>. The screen composes it with <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">--device-ui-scale</code> for component typography and geometry, while <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">--content-scale</code> applies the modifier to plugin content.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <%= framework_heading(4, 'Affected Properties') %>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              When you apply a scale modifier, it scales the following properties:
            </p>
          </div>

            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 <%= framework_list_classes %>">
            <li>Font sizes (all text elements)</li>
            <li>Line heights</li>
            <li>Component dimensions such as title bars and progress indicators</li>
            <li>Framework gaps and pixel-based spacing utilities</li>
            <li>Framework radii, text strokes, and image strokes</li>
            <li>Any custom properties that reference <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">var(--ui-scale)</code> or <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">var(--content-scale)</code></li>
          </ul>

          <div class="<%= message_sage_classes %>">
            <div class="flex items-center w-full">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 items-center">
                <%= render 'shared/icons/info' %>
              </div>
              <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-between ml-3">
                <p class="text-sm font-medium">
                  <strong>Note:</strong> Screen dimensions, percentages, container units, and physical one-pixel rails remain unchanged. Fixed pixel values emitted by framework utilities follow the selected content scale.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Combining with Device Configurations') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            Scale modifiers multiply the device's native UI scale instead of replacing it. Plugin content follows the selected modifier, while framework components also retain the device density adjustment.
            Every modifier except Regular also resolves typography to Inter Variable on low-density displays, because pixel bundles only render correctly at their native sizes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="<%= framework_docs_table_wrapper_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_docs_table_card_classes %>">
